quiz:[
{q:"The maximum escrow cushion a servicer may hold under RESPA is:",a:["One month","Two months (one-sixth of annual disbursements)","Three months","Six months"],c:1,why:"Reg X 1024.17 caps the cushion at one-sixth of estimated annual disbursements; surpluses of $50 or more must be refunded."},
{q:"A California supplemental property tax bill after purchase is:",a:["Paid by the escrow account automatically","Sent to the owner and typically not covered by the escrow account","Waived for first-time buyers","Paid by the seller"],c:1,why:"Supplemental assessments for the difference between the old and new assessed value are billed to the owner; escrow accounts are set up for the regular bill."},
{q:"A borrower may request PMI cancellation under HPA when the LTV reaches 80 percent of:",a:["Current appraised value","The original value (lower of purchase price or original appraisal)","The county assessed value","The loan amount"],c:1,why:"HPA uses original value; current-value cancellation is a separate GSE servicing option with seasoning and appraisal requirements."},
{q:"Under Reg X, a servicer may not make the first notice or filing for foreclosure until the borrower is more than:",a:["30 days delinquent","60 days delinquent","90 days delinquent","120 days delinquent"],c:3,why:"The 120-day rule gives borrowers time to apply for loss mitigation before foreclosure begins."},
{q:"A payment deferral moves missed payments to:",a:["The next three payments","A non-interest-bearing balance due at payoff or maturity","A second lien with interest","The escrow account"],c:1,why:"Agency payment deferrals create a deferred balance with no interest, due when the loan pays off, sells, or matures, without changing the regular payment."},
{q:"In California non-judicial foreclosure, after the notice of default the borrower has a reinstatement period of at least:",a:["30 days","60 days","Three months before a notice of sale can be recorded","One year"],c:2,why:"The notice of sale cannot record until three months after the NOD, and the borrower may reinstate up to five business days before the sale."},
{q:"A past client facing foreclosure asks you to negotiate with the servicer for a $2,000 fee. You should:",a:["Accept; it is a service","Decline the fee, refer to the servicer and a HUD-approved counselor, and help evaluate options for free","Charge only after the modification is approved","Refer to a modification company that pays you a referral fee"],c:1,why:"California Civil Code 2944.7 prohibits advance fees for modification services, referral fees would violate the statute and RESPA, and the right move is free help and a counselor referral."}],
